{
  "_doc": [
    "Relationships between taxonomy skills, used by skills.match_skills (see ats/skills.py).",
    "categories: broad skill -> specific skills that are evidence FOR the broad skill (partial credit,",
    "  config.CATEGORY_MATCH_CREDIT). Direction matters: MySQL supports an SQL requirement, but generic SQL",
    "  never proves MySQL. Members may themselves be categories (one extra level is followed).",
    "related: groups of skills that are related but NOT interchangeable (no credit; shown to the reviewer).",
    "  Siblings in a category and a member's own category are related automatically.",
    "Equivalent names (abbreviations, spellings, acronyms) belong in skill_taxonomy.json as aliases, not here.",
    "Every name is resolved through the taxonomy, so aliases may be used on either side.",
    "conflicts: surface form -> nearby words (within ~80 chars) that mean the name is used in another sense,",
    "  so it is not evidence (\"emr\" next to \"aws\" is Amazon EMR, not electronic medical records)."
  ],
